───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Attributions for model inputs and methodology references
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The LARM model incorporates concepts and threshold references from the
following external sources. LARM itself is an independent work and is
NOT endorsed, certified, or approved by any of these organizations.

  - Open-Meteo (https://open-meteo.com) — Weather data API (CC-BY 4.0 /
    free tier; commercial tier for production use).

  - ECMWF (European Centre for Medium-Range Weather Forecasts) — ERA5
    reanalysis (Copernicus Climate Change Service, CC-BY 4.0) and
    ensemble forecast references.

  - CWA (Central Weather Administration, Taiwan, 交通部中央氣象署) —
    Optional integration with F-D0047 township forecast and O-A0003-001
    real-time station observations. Usage requires a valid CWA Open Data
    API key. LARM is independent of and not endorsed by the CWA.

  - JMA (Japan Meteorological Agency) — Optional cross-validation data
    via Open-Meteo. LARM is independent of and not endorsed by the JMA.

  - JARUS SORA 2.5 (Joint Authorities for Rulemaking on Unmanned Systems)
    — Ground risk consequence methodology and M1-series mitigation
    concepts are inspired by the SORA 2.5 specification. LARM's
    implementation is a derivative interpretation and is NOT a SORA 2.5
    certified tool.

  - AMS Glossary of Meteorology (American Meteorological Society) —
    Terminology references for turbulence (EDR), instability indices,
    and wind regime classification.

